# Reviewable ISO 11783-10 Task Controller DDOP corpus.
#
# Object records open with the 3-byte ASCII Table ID of Tables A.1-A.5
# ("DVC", "DET", "DPD", "DPT", "DVP"), not a 1-byte numeric tag. These vectors
# were re-derived when that was corrected; the Table ID itself is spec-derived,
# the remaining field order is still the encoder's own and wants an external
# oracle (see PLAN.md G1/G2).
# Values are raw DDOP object-pool byte streams in compact hexadecimal.

# F7 — A.7 Figure A.1 puts the DeviceObject at ObjectId 0, and A.3 requires
# exactly one DeviceElement of type device numbered 0. This vector had the
# device at ObjectId 1 and no device-type element at all, so it was never a
# valid pool. The only byte changes are that ObjectId and the inserted root
# DET record; every other field is untouched.
sprayer_one_section_all_object_types=4456430000075370726179657203312E30000000000000000007534E2D313233340102030405060708090A0B0C0D0E44455401000107537072617965720000000000004445540200040253310500010002000A0014004450440A003412000503504431FFFF4450541400CDABD6FFFFFF0550726F7031FFFF4456501E00640000006F12833A03016D
# F7 — the DeviceObject moved from ObjectId 1 to 0 (A.7 Figure A.1). No
# field layout changed; only that identifier.
metered_drill_two_sections_scaled_
